description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, attribute a compose's outcome to the model that DRAFTED it rather than to whichever completion happened last. THREE edits in this one file.

PLEASE NOTE THE EXECUTION ORDER, because a previous attempt was refused on a misreading of it. Edit 2 inserts 'planDraftModel = lastDraftModel;' on the line AFTER 'planRaw = await llmCallWithFailover(...)'. That statement therefore runs only once the plan call's await has RESOLVED. llmCall assigns lastDraftModel during that very call, so at the moment planDraftModel is assigned, lastDraftModel holds the PLAN call's model - not an earlier call's. Any spec-refine call at line 4042 happens before the plan call and is overwritten by it. The refusal reasoning that lastDraftModel 'will still reflect the last LLM call made prior to the plan decomposition' describes what would happen if the capture ran BEFORE the await; it runs after.

Edit 1 declares the variable. Replace this comment line, which occurs exactly once:
// arm's outcome once its verdict is known.

with exactly:
// arm's outcome once the compose verdict is settled. planDraftModel pins the PLAN
// call's model: it is assigned AFTER that call's await resolves, so it captures the
// model that served the plan, not an earlier one.
let planDraftModel = "";

Edit 2 captures the plan model. Replace these two consecutive lines, which occur exactly once, leaving BOTH unchanged and inserting one new line between them:
      planRaw = await llmCallWithFailover(llmEndpoints, decomposePrompt(spec, maxOps, grounding, principles + composeLessons, priorFeedback, netNewTargets), model);
    } catch (e) {

with exactly:
      planRaw = await llmCallWithFailover(llmEndpoints, decomposePrompt(spec, maxOps, grounding, principles + composeLessons, priorFeedback, netNewTargets), model);
      planDraftModel = lastDraftModel;
    } catch (e) {

Edit 3 reports it, preferring the plan model. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
          model: lastDraftModel,

with exactly:
          model: planDraftModel || lastDraftModel,

Why it matters: every completion in this file shares task_type feature_compose - spec refine, plan decompose, anchor re-derivation, blind-edit repair, created-file rewrite, lint repair, and the semantic-gate JUDGE - and the judge runs after drafting, so today the arm graded for a compose is usually the judge rather than the drafter. Measured: 141 drafting-pick lines across roughly 34 composes.

The ONLY new declaration is planDraftModel in edit 1. Do NOT redeclare planRaw, lastDraftModel, model, verdict or METABOB_API_KEY, and do NOT modify any numeric literal.

